      "source_en": "Disquiet] Disgust Athenaeum 1832.\n Hell] God Nbk 14, Harvard Nbk 1, Mary Copybk 1, Athenaeum 1832, 1839. S.’s late revision, which\nremoves a word that risked giving offence and might have attracted prosecution as blasphemous, also\nalters the ironic attack of the line.\n the bride.] thy bride! Athenaeum 1832. In Nbk 14, S. originally wrote ‘thy’, then alt. it to the in\nHarvard Nbk 1.",
